| Gateway workspace key | same path, `configureInferenceCredential` | vault | state only |
| Issued API key (rotation) | `RevealSecret` host sheet / host clipboard | held per result for the active context, never persisted; retired by the review's exit (`DiscardChange` on the applied review, also before the change settles), by acknowledging the deployment, or by a context change | never |
# Inbox and reads

Source: `R2App` (`ITEMS`, `visibleItems`, `ack`, `snoozed`, `snooze`,
`inboxRows`, `sel`, `startRead`, `recheck`, `toGo`). Chunk: C30.

## Inbox

- Tabs All / Needs action / Updates / Snoozed with counts. Rows: severity
  (colour + icon + word), title, product, source line ("API keys · cached",
  "rotated 07:46"), when, acknowledged mark. Selecting opens the detail pane:
  body, facts table, "Why this matters" explanation, action button (navigates
  with context), Acknowledge / Mark as needing action, Snooze or Unsnooze.
- Empty states distinguish "first read pending" from "nothing needs action"
  and name partial sources ("3 of 6 sources were read at 07:45").
- Snooze: per item, core-computed return time, 24 hours for every item in
  P09 (the prototype's deadline-bound rotation snooze is not carried: no
  admitted operation has a grace deadline, P20). The label, toast and
  Snoozed-tab "Returns …" text all state the same time (I11). The
  `deadline` field stays optional for a future item that has a real one.
- Contextual navigation: an item's action carries a target (screen, product,
  tab, conversation). Into an ended conversation it sets a transient hint
  offering "Open the saved transcript" and "Start a new investigation".

## Reads (I4)

- `readTenant` runs a finite read of every selected product; `ReadStatus`
  carries per-product state (pending, ok, partial, needsRole), last-read
  time and counts. First read on a fresh tenant shows pending everywhere.
- Completion toast: ok "Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete" or
  warn "· 3 sources partial"; for fresh tenants "· 1 product still needs a
  role" or "· no activity yet in <tenant>". `recheckProduct` after a role is
  granted shows an info toast and re-reads.

## Core contract

- Scope `InboxItem{id, kind, severity, title, product, source, when, body,
  facts, action_target, explanation, deadline?, snooze_return?, acknowledged}`
  per tenant; intents `acknowledgeItem`, `snoozeItem`, `unsnoozeItem`,
  `readTenant`, `recheckProduct`.
- The rotation reminder (`rotation-<application>`) is a distinct item id from
  the expiry alert and clears only when the old key's deletion is read back
  (I7). Items exist only for admitted products (DESIGN-V2 §6).

## Fixtures and tests

- Board R2Inbox. Tests V2-R02, R04, R08, R09; V2-T04, T12, T13; V2-N02.
# C37 parity notes — Inbox (R2App start=inbox)

Composites: prototype board left, fixture app right, both at the window's measured web area (1440 wide on this Mac), light and dark, captured with `tools/parity/capture_app.py --chunk C37 --screen inbox --read` against the bundle in `bundle.json`. The tenant was read first, so the list carries the synthetic management plane's entries.

The board is the Inbox: the title row, the 430px list card (filter tabs with counts, rows, footer) beside the detail card. The C30 behaviour (reads, holds, the core's return time) is unchanged; only the presentation is ported.

## Deviations from the board, and why

- **Entries are the core's.** The prototype lists seven scripted items across products; the fixture tenant reads AI Runtime Security through the synthetic plane, so the rows are what that read produced. The footer's second line names the Gateway workspace only when one is chosen, else the read's first gap.
- **Severity word.** Each row's second line starts with the severity word beside the icon tile (I9); the prototype shows the icon alone.
- **The detail's primary action** is the entry's own action label from the core (for example "Open API keys"), not the prototype's generic "Open evidence"; Acknowledge toggles to "Mark as needing action" and Snooze to "Unsnooze" as in C30.
- **"Why this matters"** is the Explain banner of the prototype: shown only while the calls are shown.
- **Facts** are a definition list in three columns, as the prototype's grid.
- **Empty states** name the read (first read pending, failed, partial, nothing needs action) and offer "Open role issue" when a product needs a role, which opens that product in Administration.
- **Narrow windows.** Below the width that fits 430px beside the detail (the collapsed rail, 200% zoom) the two cards stack; the prototype is fixed-width.

## Owner's approval

Approved by the owner on 2026-10-30 ("looks good") on the composites captured after a read with the first row opened (bundle in `bundle.json`); the gate runs on that approval.
